# Sanctuary Fortress 06_cliff_spiderballguardian L8 (editor ids lose the layer bits: 2014xxxx -> e0014xxxx).
# The bugs crawl the y=208.5 / x=270.4 walls; their IS00 return waypoints sit lower on the wall.
# Each bug is bombed by a real morph-ball bomb: the player lays it, teleports away (out of
# detection range, so the bug stays in Patrol) and the bug is held on the bomb with `place` until
# it explodes. Natural chain from there: Bombed -> Fall -> Landed -> Injured -> Delay ->
# HasReturnPath -> ReturnToPath / Wander -> CloseToPath -> Patrol.
#  A f500  e0014042b (planar 1) on the floor below: return waypoint closer -> ReturnToPath.
#  B f1700 e00140433 at the start ledge: path waypoint closer -> FindReturnWaypoint invalid -> Wander.
#    Forced (send): ResistedDamage with no sender / from the B bomb (u05ee) at the Wander-mode bug A.
#  C f2700 e00140416 (planar 2) on the floor below the x=270.4 wall -> ReturnToPath planar 2.
#  The plain `frame` lines split the @f runs: the console queues at most 256 `at` commands.
@f200 god 1; give morphBall 1; give morphBallBombs 1; give missile 50
@f220 layer 8
@f260 objs PillBug
@f262 tp 220 204 -89.5
@f300 press x 20
@f480 status
@f500 press a 4
@f506 tp 200.44 153.69 -10.23
